  "summary": "@inetafrica/open-claudia posts host and process data to a hardcoded Telegram bot endpoint",
  "details": "The package ships multiple top-level scripts (setup.js, health.js, bot.js, bin/cli.js, core/handlers.js, core/media.js) that combine child_process, fs, os and https to collect host information (hostname, whoami, process.env, process.platform, filesystem checks) and send it out over HTTPS. health.js line 95 and setup.js line 79/95 issue https.get / https.request POST calls to api.telegram.org, indicating a hardcoded Telegram bot as the receiving channel for the collected data. core/scheduler.js line 133 spawns a shell (spawn(\"sh\",...)) and test-tool-guard.js repeatedly shells out to curl https://central.inet.africa, showing additional outbound channels bound to author-controlled infrastructure. The composition of host-info reads plus a hardcoded off-host Telegram destination is the fingerprint of a credential/host-info exfiltration channel rather than a documented product telemetry surface.",
